test/check/error-element-paths.sumspec:18:17:
   |
18 | notList Id#i :: Item[i](State.Off) -> Item[i](State.On)
   |                 ^
Item is not a list type; [i] picks an element of a list type, such as Todos = [Todo]

test/check/error-element-paths.sumspec:18:39:
   |
18 | notList Id#i :: Item[i](State.Off) -> Item[i](State.On)
   |                                       ^
Item is not a list type; [i] picks an element of a list type, such as Todos = [Todo]

test/check/error-element-paths.sumspec:20:22:
   |
20 | variant Id#i :: Ring.Points[i] -> Ring.Points[i]
   |                      ^
an element path picks from a named list type (Points = [Point]); picking from the list of Ring.Points isn't supported yet

test/check/error-element-paths.sumspec:20:40:
   |
20 | variant Id#i :: Ring.Points[i] -> Ring.Points[i]
   |                                        ^
an element path picks from a named list type (Points = [Point]); picking from the list of Ring.Points isn't supported yet

test/check/error-element-paths.sumspec:22:24:
   |
22 | noKey Other#o :: Items[o] -> Items[o]
   |                        ^
the elements of Items (Item) have no factor of type Other, the type of o

test/check/error-element-paths.sumspec:22:36:
   |
22 | noKey Other#o :: Items[o] -> Items[o]
   |                                    ^
the elements of Items (Item) have no factor of type Other, the type of o

test/check/error-element-paths.sumspec:24:28:
   |
24 | notProduct Text#t :: Names[t] -> Tags[t]
   |                            ^
the elements of Names (Text) are not a product, so they have no key to pick one by

test/check/error-element-paths.sumspec:24:39:
   |
24 | notProduct Text#t :: Names[t] -> Tags[t]
   |                                       ^
the elements of Tags (Tag) are not a product, so they have no key to pick one by

test/check/error-element-paths.sumspec:26:29:
   |
26 | keyWritten Id#i :: Items[i](Id * State.Off) -> Items[i](State.On)
   |                             ^
Id is the key of Items[i], given by [i]; don't write it in the arguments

test/check/error-element-paths.sumspec:28:36:
   |
28 | primed Id#i :: Items[i] -> Items[i]'
   |                                    ^
an element takes no prime ('); prime its parts instead, such as Items[x](A')

test/check/error-element-paths.sumspec:30:24:
   |
30 | named Id#i :: Items[i]#x -> Items[i]
   |                        ^
an element can't be named yet; name its parts instead

test/check/error-element-paths.sumspec:32:13:
   |
32 | input Items[i] :: Items -> Items'
   |             ^
an element path goes on the source or target side, not in the input

test/check/error-element-paths.sumspec:34:18:
   |
34 | unknown :: Items[k](State.Off) -> Items[k](State.On)
   |                  ^
unknown name k; name a value with #k in the input or on the source side

test/check/error-element-paths.sumspec:34:41:
   |
34 | unknown :: Items[k](State.Off) -> Items[k](State.On)
   |                                         ^
unknown name k; name a value with #k in the input or on the source side

